{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 562 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "41d47d7ab45c21a24c6b6d7d351499489a89159202b7df0e48b830a065e7684b" :edb/db-before-t 561 :edb/db-after-t 562 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533874 50 #inst "2026-10-05T06:37:33.771Z" 13194139533874 true] [17592186054517 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262830 13194139533874 true] [17592186054522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262847 13194139533874 true] [17592186054584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262833 13194139533874 true] [17592186059606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262840 13194139533874 true] [17592186059715 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262803 13194139533874 true] [17592186059769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262810 13194139533874 true] [17592186068681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262782 13194139533874 true] [17592186073656 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262789 13194139533874 true] [17592186083217 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262775 13194139533874 true] [17592186083301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262823 13194139533874 true] [17592186087767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262817 13194139533874 true] [17592186115849 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533874 true] [17592186115849 1145 "The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ is $x=0.$\n\nTo find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x),$ we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & =0 \\\\ -x & =-2 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186192639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262796 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262776 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1089 "q-112876" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1100 "According to the rational roots theorem, which of the following **cannot** be a root of the polynomial $f(x)=14{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}-x-7?$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1113 #uuid "6029834b-7153-5587-95c0-5adfbb9eff9b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262775 1145 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial $f(x),$ the constant term is $-7$ and the leading coefficient is $14.$ So, any rational roots of $f(x)$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of }-7}{\\text{factor of }14}.\n$$\n\nOf the given answer choices, only $\\frac{1}{21}$ does not take the above form. The denominator $(21)$ is not a factor of $14.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262777 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262778 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262779 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262780 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262781 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262778 13194139533874 true] [17592186262776 1110 #uuid "1f68bd25-2d3e-5bc1-b52a-7f474271c701" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262777 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262777 1111 #uuid "bdf7a7e2-c83d-5d7f-a3be-d03c4fd46a56" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262778 1034 "\\frac{1}{21}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262778 1111 #uuid "d8542cc2-cb0a-5cf8-84ad-40437a5be95e" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262779 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262779 1111 #uuid "5100696c-1323-5af2-94ba-f71d4f2e601b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262780 1034 "7" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262780 1111 #uuid "45e3514d-7e1e-5a50-aec2-37cd36d7b91c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262781 1034 "-1" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262781 1111 #uuid "af67276e-0858-58f6-8d90-ce34dfe7c0ca" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262783 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1089 "q-113296" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1100 "Given that $\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}=t$ and $\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v}=r,$ what is $t+r?$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1113 #uuid "94656d5b-5501-55b7-ac7e-cff2be11bd02" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262782 1145 "We wish to add the following fractions:\n\n$$\nt+r=\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $2(3+2v)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3-5v}{3+2v} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{2(3-5v)}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v+2(3-5v)}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v+6-10v}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6-3v}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(2-v)}{2(3+2v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262784 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262785 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262786 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262787 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262788 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262788 13194139533874 true] [17592186262783 1110 #uuid "9bce0baa-80ba-5fc5-88d2-880f32116a15" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262784 1034 "\\frac{2(3+v)}{3+2v}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262784 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262784 1111 #uuid "48fd37dc-102e-54db-bbfb-3a2cbcc44c92" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262785 1034 "\\frac{3+8v}{3+2v}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262785 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262785 1111 #uuid "181b05a4-3d83-5761-af97-acbe6f928228" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262786 1034 "\\frac{3-8v}{2(3+2v)}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262786 1111 #uuid "854c750f-32a8-56e1-a054-75899195a266" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262787 1034 "\\frac{5-8v}{2(3+2v)}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262787 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262787 1111 #uuid "76c40b6e-aa86-56c9-b41d-570a2e53d136" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262788 1034 "\\frac{3(2-v)}{2(3+2v)}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262788 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262788 1111 #uuid "04b6c341-9c7f-57c4-887d-d97df4a836d1" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262790 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1089 "q-13616" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949162/assets/afef278ec13dda23227ef9dc28b0e5f3240a0481eaca208fa3b2d3ba27c85537.png)\n\nGiven that $(-1,4)$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, find the coordinates of $P.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1113 #uuid "60e5d36c-88c0-5cf7-8b86-f1dd3ac9a6db" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262789 1145 "The given points are ${{(2,2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(a,b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(-1,4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (-1,4) & =(\\frac{2+a}{2},\\frac{2+b}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-1=\\frac{2+a}{2} \\\\ 4=\\frac{2+b}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}a=-4 \\\\ b=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $(a,b)=(-4,6).$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262791 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262792 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262793 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262794 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262795 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262791 13194139533874 true] [17592186262790 1110 #uuid "6884fa24-6da2-5e75-be16-32f1846cdd2c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262791 1034 "(-4,6)" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262791 1111 #uuid "3ce325be-d2cc-5441-8328-1ef2bf8bd000" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262792 1034 "(-4,-6)" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262792 1111 #uuid "8e0f401a-6d08-5342-9a9a-4b3cc5fe0f66" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262793 1034 "(-4,9)" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262793 1111 #uuid "6b324b87-3037-5239-8380-00230f914382" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262794 1034 "(6,4)" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262794 1111 #uuid "ecb4ed72-5fee-5e6e-a9ce-13185b0825a8" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262795 1034 "(-4,7)" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262795 1111 #uuid "bf89ce8c-3dad-532f-8eff-ff87b00f8adf" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262797 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1089 "q-148434" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1100 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{4}{7x-1}.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1113 #uuid "04d4cf54-a7a9-55d6-92f9-191eb3416f50" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262796 1145 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4}{7x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4}{7y-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{4}{7y-1} \\\\ x(7y-1) & =4 \\\\ 7xy-x & =4 \\\\ 7xy & =x+4 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x+4}{7x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+4}{7x}.\n$$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262798 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262799 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262800 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262801 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262802 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262799 13194139533874 true] [17592186262797 1110 #uuid "4ce0241a-c33b-5946-a90a-9bf8729d04bb" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262798 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4-x}{7x}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262798 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262798 1111 #uuid "2c0dbc63-1dfb-5bf0-9f00-fe5408d36e0b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262799 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+4}{7x}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262799 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262799 1111 #uuid "903f8109-394b-53d0-bf6c-7ddf61ca7bc9" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262800 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{7x+1}{4x}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262800 1111 #uuid "c253899b-067d-52fa-a7bc-3f9ba3f43b64" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262801 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+4}{7x}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262801 1111 #uuid "cb8994dc-e439-5191-9a3d-16ccf536d7c9" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262802 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+7}{7x}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262802 1111 #uuid "a00400d3-3ab1-5ee7-9dfa-4db1a0a614a6" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262804 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1089 "q-1780" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1100 "Suppose you have $5$ shirts, $4$ pants, and $9$ ties. How many outfits can be made consisting of a shirt, pants, and a tie?" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1113 #uuid "3217b938-6776-57d3-a045-a78f82513de9" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262803 1145 "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of outfits} & =\\text{Number of shirts} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pants} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of ties} \\\\  & =5\\times 4\\times 9 \\\\  & =180.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $180$ different outfits can be made consisting of a shirt, pants, and a tie." 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262805 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262806 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262807 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262808 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262809 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262806 13194139533874 true] [17592186262804 1110 #uuid "b380d71c-d89a-5821-8fd0-a2bebb0985dd" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262805 1034 "270" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262805 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262805 1111 #uuid "a89d47d6-7d72-539d-916d-d2a4b0a4e73b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262806 1034 "180" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262806 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262806 1111 #uuid "ea32e158-9dc8-5e64-ab79-c0914e460f30" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262807 1034 "9" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262807 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262807 1111 #uuid "9b00320c-eb84-5c33-bdd7-56ce148f1604" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262808 1034 "81" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262808 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262808 1111 #uuid "f85dba1c-97d6-53e6-baec-d3a6a5c0071b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262809 1034 "18" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262809 1111 #uuid "a7514173-15bd-5344-ac61-60534909e8cc" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262811 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1089 "q-23386" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1100 "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1113 #uuid "75a1ef17-bd84-5a6f-a321-ae3c8b53dee2" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262810 1145 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949162/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}).$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262812 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262813 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262814 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262815 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262816 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262815 13194139533874 true] [17592186262811 1110 #uuid "5435d141-7257-5935-83ed-ac313c47213c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262812 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262812 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262812 1111 #uuid "a3b70270-c393-57a1-b8e3-b392ff96a715" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262813 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262813 1111 #uuid "5c4c9fe2-02c0-57c4-9f0a-4478a046fc10" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262814 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262814 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262814 1111 #uuid "baa0a422-393e-5847-b089-8e6c730e03b3" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262815 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262815 1111 #uuid "6b80b6a9-d7e9-5960-88f6-32f69484a819" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262816 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262816 1111 #uuid "76c19521-0ced-57a7-9440-b0815b56bae5" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262818 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262821 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1089 "q-250543" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1100 "Solve the equation ${x}^{2}-12x+40=0.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\pm $\n{{field-2}}$\\text{i}$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1113 #uuid "c0f5813f-1311-5202-9907-b6bbfa128b38" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262817 1145 "We can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=1,\\,b=-12,$ and $c=40.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^{2}-4(1)(40)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{144-160}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=6+2\\text{i}$ and $x=6-2\\text{i}.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262819 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262820 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1041 "field-1" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262819 13194139533874 true] [17592186262818 1110 #uuid "abf388ef-d094-558a-94c3-1e372d97c0a5" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262819 1034 "6" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262819 1111 #uuid "9515f7da-b1dc-51db-b689-f0977d4f5c5c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262820 1034 "-6" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262820 1111 #uuid "4ce518d5-82cb-56e3-8acd-2caa5157f5d8" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262822 13194139533874 true] [17592186262821 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533874 true] [17592186262821 1041 "field-2" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262821 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262822 13194139533874 true] [17592186262821 1110 #uuid "84030060-d5c1-5f90-aaed-3632ab2d0ef9" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262822 1034 "2" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262822 1111 #uuid "5c3b0258-b5ba-59da-9790-f68d61b80f8c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262824 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1089 "q-288821" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1100 "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+427x-58\\,971=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1113 #uuid "943b524b-b2a3-5844-86ae-8628c6825604" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262823 1145 "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=1,\\,b=427,\\,c=-58\\,971.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{(-58\\,971)}{1}=-58\\,971.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262825 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262826 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262827 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262828 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262829 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262829 13194139533874 true] [17592186262824 1110 #uuid "d4ef662f-a053-5e72-9509-a0921088d28c" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262825 1034 "\\frac{427}{2}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262825 1111 #uuid "650d1dd7-08da-540b-86ac-5ae2c13762e1" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262826 1034 "58\\,971" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262826 1111 #uuid "e0f4ca59-de3e-5472-a5d0-95413f861c9b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262827 1034 "(-2)\\cdot 58\\,971" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262827 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262827 1111 #uuid "164d42bb-31a8-5e23-bb63-95ad62ce46e5" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262828 1034 "\\frac{-58\\,971}{427}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262828 1111 #uuid "2f574de3-cd2a-50bc-93a3-4159ffc99be3" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262829 1034 "-58\\,971" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262829 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262829 1111 #uuid "959fb719-9d81-539a-a680-dc3eba45ac90" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262831 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1089 "q-338396" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1100 "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1113 #uuid "b02345e9-0e5e-51b9-851e-2fb58ece83fd" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262830 1145 "Applying the root and quotient rules, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{3})}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{2}-4x+5)}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator separately. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{3}) & ={2}^{3} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{2}-4x+5) & ={2}^{2}-4(2)+5 \\\\  & =4-8+5 \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{3})}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({x}^{2}-4x+5)}} & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{8}{1}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262832 13194139533874 true] [17592186262831 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533874 true] [17592186262831 1041 "field-1" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262831 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262832 13194139533874 true] [17592186262831 1110 #uuid "45d17601-5212-57fc-81a0-98a67cf0c81b" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262832 1034 "2" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262832 1111 #uuid "2e330232-ea69-5e4d-8860-2f98ad26449f" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262834 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1089 "q-61203" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1100 "What is the sixth term of the following sequence?\n\n$$\nf(n+2)=f(n+1)+f(n)\\,,\\,f(1)=-4\\,,\\,f(2)=-1,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1113 #uuid "f33f273d-36a2-559f-8e4a-6a2268d64069" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262833 1145 "The sixth term is represented by $f(6).$\n\nTo compute $f(6),$ we first need to compute $f(3).$ So, we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+2) & =f(n+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(1+2) & =f(1+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =(-4)+(-1) \\\\ f(3) & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to compute $f(4),$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2+2) & =f(2+1)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =(-5)+(-1) \\\\ f(4) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe continue this process to compute $f(5)$ and $f(6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =f(4)+f(3)=(-6)+(-5)=-11 \\\\ f(6) & =f(5)+f(4)=(-11)+(-6)=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sixth term of the sequence is $f(6)=-17.$" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262835 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262836 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262837 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262838 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262839 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262838 13194139533874 true] [17592186262834 1110 #uuid "fe064f1e-34bf-5a7e-bb53-e1ade0fca113" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262835 1034 "-11" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262835 1111 #uuid "548840ce-bd20-5b10-b50f-a91b7d7ea091" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262836 1034 "11" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262836 1111 #uuid "6cf41f36-7699-53b6-b5d6-ba4baa4e09fd" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262837 1034 "8" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262837 1111 #uuid "5cdb7f24-414d-5683-bda0-8ab1db998a69" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262838 1034 "-17" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262838 1111 #uuid "ca507321-c66c-52b0-9ef9-342aa994b2cc" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262839 1034 "0" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533874 true] [17592186262839 1111 #uuid "ae7d6a32-9f79-595f-9701-65d1479b2a84" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262841 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1089 "q-64675" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1100 "The angle $\\theta =-{395}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1113 #uuid "44ac753e-1a93-50f3-a318-c664d2c32040" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262840 1145 "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{395}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{395}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-{35}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{395}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={325}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${325}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{395}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949162/assets/936e222cebb005bc504867f26eb2144bb976cab2441e53051121e056be158be1.png)\n\nWe see that ${325}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant IV. Therefore, $-{395}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262842 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262843 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262844 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262845 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262846 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1041 "selection" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262844 13194139533874 true] [17592186262841 1110 #uuid "6d1d837e-4fe2-5e72-9a0e-b0299bf13fa4" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262842 1034 "II" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533874 true] [17592186262842 1111 #uuid "d5925800-3583-5be3-96c8-f946d72bc2af" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262843 1034 "III" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533874 true] [17592186262843 1111 #uuid "47e0f7a8-cc9e-5974-9a39-877364e06d66" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262844 1034 "IV" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533874 true] [17592186262844 1111 #uuid "b1944c40-c2c1-58d9-a917-5856de87e6b0" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262845 1034 "I" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533874 true] [17592186262845 1111 #uuid "e13f9f1f-d973-5f0f-a1e2-78cc78ad8f90" 13194139533874 true] [17592186262846 1034 "Between quadran